ory; a ''transitional'' process.—'''3.''' Specifically, in ''art'', relating to, characterizing, or belonging to an epoch or stage of change from one style or state of development to the next succeeding, and especially to that between archaism and full development in Greek art, and to that between the Romanesque and the Pointed in medieval art.—'''Transitional epithelium.''' {{smaller|See ''epithelium''.}}

